# The machine going off (design 4.9), the first of two runs. A program with
# something not saved holds it: after 5 seconds a panel names the program, and
# 取消 goes back to the session. The program's own question is then answered. Then a
# window that keeps something when asked to close, a process without a window,
# and one that ignores being told to end. Run with --keep-disk and then
# ui_shutdown2.steps on the disk kept. The buttons' places come from the panel's
# size and the first window's (off_panel).
open 019b54a4-6ccf-72f7-e320-c98e4a0bab4e
expect calc: ready
wait 800
click 200 163
text 77
key 28
wait 300
logmark
poweroff
expectsincein 15 has not closed
wait 500
click 664 441
expectsincein 10 the person cancelled the going off
wait 500
ready
key 28
expectsincein 30 calc: saved
sdnstart
win ktsdn
logmark
poweroff
expectsincein 15 programs asked to end, 0 not ended
expectsince shutdown: 2 processes told to end
expectsincein 20 has not ended: ended by force
expectsincein 20 shutdown: after force, 0 processes left
expectsincein 20 TessronOS desktop: turning the machine off
expectsincein 20 marked clean
expectsincein 20 mounts taken down
